{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_structure_cannot_force_concentration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.graded_structure_cannot_force_concentration","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L291-L328","doc":"**THE CRUX (limitative — bean `qou-7ygi`).**  A single structural dichotomy\nsettles the graded route.  Package it as: there are two graded assignments\n`single = G_λ` and `fake = H_λ` (`H_λ` = the honest jet-order / coinvariant\nTOWER, the genuine graded object the substrate produces) such that, on every\nnon-trivial block,\n\n  • BOTH carry the ungraded Wedderburn dimension `dim V_λ` (`same_total`);\n  • `H_λ` is a two-parity multiplicity space, so its signed Euler characteristic\n    CANCELS strictly below `dim` and never equals `Δ_λ` (`fake_ne`);\n  • `G_λ` is the cancellation-free single-parity object and DOES equal `Δ_λ`\n    (`single_is`);\n  • and — the general reason (`realization_forces_single_parity`) — ANY graded\n    object realizing `Δ_λ` must be cancellation-free (single grade-parity),\n    i.e. the top-cohomology concentration, not a genuine multiplicity grading.\n\nSince every algebraic substrate grading (jet-order/coinvariant tower, KLR in the\nsemisimple regime, Demazure) is a genuine graded multiplicity space — mass at\nboth parities — none forces `G_λ`.  The single-degree concentration\n`H^{2n(λ)}(𝓑_λ) = V_λ` (Springer 1978) is a GEOMETRIC categorification input the\n13 drivers do not supply.  The NEGATIVE answer to `qou-7ygi`, unifying the\ncount (#4559) / SDP (#4570) / valuation (#4574) negatives under one mechanism:\nCANCELLATION. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_cancels_ne_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_cancels_ne_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L279-L287","doc":"**`H_λ` can never equal `Δ_λ`** — because it cancels below `dim = |Δ_λ|`.\nThe honest coinvariant / jet-order TOWER does NOT realize the binding factor;\nthe concentration is genuinely absent from it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_abs_altSum_lt_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_abs_altSum_lt_dim","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L271-L277","doc":"**`H_λ` strictly undershoots**: `|χ(H_λ)| < dim V_λ` on every non-trivial block\n— the cancellation, quantified. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_both_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_both_parity","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L261-L269","doc":"**`H_λ` (the honest jet-order / coinvariant TOWER) is two-parity** on every\nnon-trivial block: it carries positive mass at BOTH an even and an odd grade.\nTHIS is the cancellation source — a genuine graded multiplicity space spreads\n`V_λ` across a run of consecutive grades, hitting both parities.  (The two\ndim-1 blocks are single monomials `q^0`, `q^{10}` — vacuously single-parity —\nhence the `dim ≠ 1` hypothesis.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.single_is_single_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.single_is_single_parity","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L254-L259","doc":"**`G_λ` is cancellation-free** — all its mass sits on one grade-parity\n(`E=0` or `O=0`), matching the general characterization: the concentrated\ntop-cohomology object saturates the `|χ| = dim` ceiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.single_altSum_eq_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.single_altSum_eq_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L248-L250","doc":"`G_λ` realizes `Δ_λ` (the #4553 single-degree collapse). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_sum_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_sum_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L245-L246","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.single_sum_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.single_sum_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L241-L243","doc":"Both objects carry the ungraded Wedderburn dimension `dim V_λ` (`f_λ(1)=dim`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaLambda_realization_is_cancellation_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaLambda_realization_is_cancellation_free","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L212-L231","doc":"**THE FRONTIER (general, sorry-free).**  Any graded object `l` whose ungraded\ntotal is the Wedderburn dimension `dim V_λ` and whose signed Euler\ncharacteristic is the binding factor `Δ_λ` is necessarily CANCELLATION-FREE:\nall its mass sits on a single grade-parity (`E(l)=0 ∨ O(l)=0`).  Contrapositive:\na graded object with mass at BOTH parities — every genuine coinvariant / jet-\norder / KLR multiplicity space — can NEVER equal `Δ_λ`.  The single-degree\ntop-cohomology object is the canonical cancellation-free realization; the honest\ntower `H_λ` is excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_deltaLambda_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_deltaLambda_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L208-L210","doc":"`|Δ_λ| = dim V_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_altSum_eq_sum_of_single_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_altSum_eq_sum_of_single_parity","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L187-L197","doc":"**Single-parity objects SATURATE the ceiling.** If all mass sits on one\ngrade-parity (`E=0` or `O=0` — cancellation-free), then `|χ(l)| = Σ l[i]`.\nThe single-degree top-cohomology object `G_λ` is of this form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_altSum_lt_sum_of_both_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_altSum_lt_sum_of_both_parity","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L176-L185","doc":"**CANCELLATION is strict under two-parity support.** If a graded object carries\npositive mass at BOTH an even and an odd grade, its signed Euler characteristic\nstrictly undershoots the total: `|χ(l)| < Σ l[i]`.  This is the single mechanism\nbehind every \"does-not-force-concentration\" negative — a genuine graded\nmultiplicity space cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_altSum_le_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_altSum_le_sum","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L170-L174","doc":"**The total dimension is the ceiling on `|χ|`.** `|χ(l)| ≤ Σ l[i]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sum_eq_masses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sum_eq_masses","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L156-L162","doc":"`Σ l[i] = E(l) + O(l)`: the ungraded total is even mass plus odd mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.altSum_eq_masses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.altSum_eq_masses","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L147-L154","doc":"`χ(l) = E(l) − O(l)`: the signed Euler characteristic is even mass minus odd\nmass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.masses_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.masses_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L139-L145","doc":"Both masses are nonnegative (sums of dimensions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.masses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.masses","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L132-L137","doc":"**Even-graded / odd-graded mass** of a graded object, as a pair\n`(E(l), O(l))`: `E(l) = Σ_{i even} l[i]`, `O(l) = Σ_{i odd} l[i]`.\nA cons shifts every grade up by one, so the even/odd roles swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.altSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.altSum","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaGradedConcentration.lean#L128-L130","signatureChunk":0}]}